From 8271a07c293af6d9f0403c062b3e0251c2309a03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 20:38:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: fix MLO per-link RCPI/traffic-stats queries and TLV
 0xa2 aggregation

TLV 0x96 (Associated STA Link Metrics) and TLV 0xe4 (Affiliated STA
Metrics) queried a guessed nested netlink attribute (ID 31) on a
derived "parent MLD interface" to get per-affiliated-link signal and
traffic counters. That attribute's sub-fields always read back zero on
this driver, so both affiliated links of an MLO client collapsed onto
the same fallback RCPI.

Replace it with a direct nl80211 GET_STATION query per affiliated
link, issued on that link's own per-link BSS interface for that link's
own STA MAC, reusing the existing bwl::nl80211_client::get_sta_info()
already used for non-MLO stations.

Also fix TLV 0xe4 emitting up to 3x too many entries for a multi-BSS
AP MLD: its dedup set was checked against the outer response entry's
STA MAC before expanding to affiliated links, but that MAC differs
across BSS iterations for the same MLD, so every new value re-emitted
all affiliated links again. Move the dedup to per affiliated-link MAC,
matching the TLV 0x96 handling.

Fix is_sta_reported_bssid_valid() on the controller to resolve an
affiliated link MAC to its MLD station the same way
dm_set_sta_link_metrics() already does, so per-link TLV 0x96 entries
are no longer rejected before they reach the data model.

Finally, fix TLV 0xa2 (Associated STA Traffic Stats) not matching the
true MLD-level aggregate: each monitor only reports the traffic it
observes on its own BSS/link, so an MLO STA present on multiple
monitors was previously deduped by keeping only the first monitor's
partial report and discarding the rest. Replace the presence-only
dedup set with an accumulator that sums byte/packet/error counters
across every monitor call in a query round, so the emitted TLV 0xa2
reflects the true MLD-level aggregate.

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
